# Coverage options for `dotnet test`, shared by the ci and sonar workflows: `dotnet test ... '@coverage.rsp'`.
# Keep the quotes: unquoted, PowerShell parses @coverage as its splatting operator.
#
# Drives the coverlet.MTP extension (referenced by every test project) to emit OpenCover XML. SonarQube /
# SonarCloud reads C# coverage from OpenCover via sonar.cs.opencover.reportsPaths; it does not consume
# coverlet's default Cobertura output. Keeping the options here rather than in each workflow means local runs
# and CI produce identical reports.
#
# Command-line options, not a testconfig.json: a coverlet configuration file is authoritative and switches
# off coverlet's default exclusions (generated and compiler-generated code, ExcludeFromCodeCoverage, the test
# assemblies themselves), which these options keep and only extend with Obsolete.
--coverlet
--coverlet-output-format
opencover
--coverlet-exclude-by-attribute
Obsolete
